<sect1 id="chapter3_1autotoc_md95_1s1"><sect2 id="chapter3_1autotoc_md95">
<title>SMT result semantics</title><para><computeroutput>SMTSolveResult</computeroutput> supports <computeroutput>Sat</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>Unsat</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>Unknown</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>SMTModel</computeroutput> currently stores bindings as textual items. The model representation can evolve without invalidating this basic contract.</para>
<para><programlisting filename=".text"><codeline><highlight class="normal">class<sp/>MySMTSolver<sp/>:<sp/>public<sp/>sattyre::SMTSolver<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">public:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>void<sp/>load(const<sp/>sattyre::SMTProblem&amp;<sp/>problem)<sp/>override<sp/>{<sp/>text_<sp/>=<sp/>problem.smtlib;<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>sattyre::SMTSolveResult<sp/>solve()<sp/>override<sp/>{<sp/>return<sp/>sattyre::SMTSolveResult::Unknown;<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>sattyre::SMTModel<sp/>model()<sp/>const<sp/>override<sp/>{<sp/>return<sp/>{};<sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">private:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>std::string<sp/>text_;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">};</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
